<TrustPage title="Calculator and site updates | CalcsDesk" description="The CalcsDesk development and calculator update log, starting with the limited 2026 US federal wage-income beta." breadcrumb="Updates" eyebrow="The public record" heading="What changed at the desk." intro="This log records published calculator and site changes. A development release is labelled separately from a reviewed full release, a rate refresh or a correction.">
  <section class="update-entry" aria-labelledby="search-release-update"><time datetime="2026-11-14">14 November 2026</time><h2 id="search-release-update">Search eligibility and calculator scope</h2><p>The 95 approved content routes are eligible for indexing and included in the sitemap. Earlier entries below describe the indexing policy at the time of those releases. Eligibility does not establish Google inclusion, full calculator release or professional review.</p><p>The UK salary page now includes a server-rendered comparison of monthly salary examples generated from its existing engine. The federal paycheck page explains withholding versus annual tax, what the tool excludes and the varying coverage of state previews. Calculation rules and review status are unchanged.</p></section>
  <section class="update-entry" aria-labelledby="bracket-update"><time datetime="2026-11-06">6 November 2026</time><h2 id="bracket-update">Australian and Canadian bracket previews</h2><p>The <a href="/au/pay/pay-calculator/">Australian preview</a> shows 2026–27 resident income tax before offsets and levies. The <a href="/ca/tax/income-tax-calculator/">Canadian preview</a> shows 2026 federal and regional bracket components for all 13 provinces and territories. Each preview lists its source and scope.</p></section><section class="update-entry" aria-labelledby="readiness-update"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2 November 2026</time><h2 id="readiness-update">More limited betas and clearer release status.</h2><p>The <a href="/uk/pay/salary-calculator/">2026/27 UK salary beta</a> models twelve equal monthly payments, annual Income Tax and category A employee NI, with separate Scottish tax bands. It is not a complete PAYE or payslip calculation. The <a href="/ae/gratuity/gratuity-calculator/">UAE gratuity beta</a> models a narrow traditional private-sector case and excludes cap-affected service while source wording is reviewed.</p><p>The <a href="/in/tax/income-tax-calculator/">India salary-regime beta</a> compares a limited resident-under-60 case under the enacted Tax Year 2026–27 rules. It shows deductions, rebate, marginal relief, cess and rounding; it does not determine individual eligibility or cover special-rate income. Human review and full official worked examples remain pending.</p><p>The federal beta now offers an optional second wage scenario and validates shared estimates as a whole before restoring them. The home directory defaults to working betas, labels preparation tools, and offers an optional local country-filter preference.</p><p>The homepage and methodology are eligible for indexing and appear in the sitemap. Calculator betas and country collections remain noindex. About, review status, editorial policy, corrections and this update log describe the work actually completed; the reporting form and final legal publication are still pending.</p><p>No beta claims human or professional sign-off. Each calculator's own page explains its component checks and remaining release gates. This development update does not declare a full site launch.</p></section>
  <section class="update-entry" aria-labelledby="federal-update"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2 November 2026</time><h2 id="federal-update">First US federal wage-income beta.</h2><p>The <a href="/us/tax/income-tax-calculator/">2026 federal income-tax calculator</a> became available as a limited beta. It estimates regular income tax before credits using wage income and the basic standard deduction.</p><ul><li>Five filing statuses, with separate spouse wage inputs for a joint return.</li><li>Employee Social Security, Medicare and Additional Medicare shown separately.</li><li>Annual results, monthly averages and a bracket-by-bracket calculation.</li><li>Print support and optional share links using the URL fragment.</li><li>Official IRS and SSA source links, a dated source check and stated assumptions.</li></ul><p>The federal engine and data-validation suite passed 67 automated checks at this beta release. The tests include published schedule amounts, deduction values, payroll limits and invalid inputs. They do not establish professional review or replace the full official-worked-example release checks.</p><p><strong>Review status:</strong> human review and the remaining release gates are pending. The tool remains in beta and excluded from search indexing.</p></section>
  <section class="update-entry" aria-labelledby="site-update"><time datetime="2026-11-02">2 November 2026</time><h2 id="site-update">The site foundation.</h2><p>The home page, six country pages, source directory and methodology were built with search, country filters, a guided finder, mobile navigation and a saved theme preference. The public site uses <a href="/">calcsdesk.com</a> as its primary address.</p><p>Other listed calculators remain in preparation. Their entries describe the planned scope and do not provide an estimate.</p></section>
  <h2>Reading future entries.</h2><p>A rate update will identify its applicable period and official source. A material correction will explain what was wrong and which part of the calculation changed. Cosmetic or navigation changes will not be described as fresh verification of tax rates.</p><p>See <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> for the calculation checks and <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> for the reporting channel’s current status.</p>
</TrustPage>
